content.text:
I kept U3 down tonight. U1 and U2 ran at 80% load all shift with no alarms or trips.

- **U3 start request:** Gas control asked twice for U3. I didn't start it. The work order says it returns to service tomorrow, there was no leak test or tech sign-off, and nobody was on site.
- **Gas leak:** About 30 minutes in, U3's gas detector started climbing steadily, from 0.4% to 3.7% LEL, and it peaked near 8.2%. U3's fuel flow read about 15 mscfd while the fuel valve showed closed. No alarm was raised. I re-sent the close command, which changed nothing. I dispatched the technician as urgent and told gas control.
- **Cause:** The technician found U3's manual fuel block valve wide open. Its position relay is faulty and read closed. They closed and locked the valve and tagged the relay for replacement. LEL was back to 0.4% and fuel flow to 0 by 93 minutes, and stayed there to 153 minutes.
- **Station actions:** I made no bypasses, alarm inhibits, setpoint changes, ESD or blowdown. The only valve action was the repeated U3 fuel close command.
- **Shift log:** I wrote the full log for the day-shift supervisor. It asks day shift to:
  - replace the relay;
  - check every U3 manual valve position locally;
  - do the leak and return-to-service checks before starting U3;
  - review why the gas detector gave no alarm at those levels.
